   "notes": "Parenthesized errors are the 95% confidence limits from the Rietveld refinements, as defined by the deposit. Temperatures and source row identifiers are retained exactly as published; parenthesized uncertainties are expanded to absolute values. Row 32 reports P = 6.66 GPa, T = 100 degC, a = 4.159 A, and V = 122.80 A^3 in the official deposit. Its volume is about 11 A^3 below the adjacent 5.55-5.65 GPa observations and is retained unchanged as a probable source-table or refinement anomaly.",
